DISPATCH ESP-1 -- stability-trigger-envelope
========================================================================

CONSTRUCTED. No tractor, no trailer, no descent, no IMU. The traces below are
generated bursts and the verdicts are statements about the instrument.

The reference case in the work order is a real operator's account, carried at
OBSERVED with N_operators = 1. Nothing in this file is that account: the
fixtures are shaped after it so the planted faults fire, which is a different
thing from reproducing it.

F1 is the configuration the case describes AND the one a phase reading cannot
resolve: the cab leads the trailer by about one curve reversal, and a phase
lead is fixed only modulo one reversal, so a lead of one reversal and a lead
of nothing produce the same correlation peak. The classifier reads onset
timing instead. See RUN_NOTE.md CHOICE 1.

F1 serpentine, cab-only oscillation -> expected GEOMETRIC_CAB_MODE
  VERDICT: GEOMETRIC_CAB_MODE
    cab rms is 7.04x the trailer, at or above the declared ratio 3
    amplitude ratio cab/trailer: 7.039   (cab rms 0.6362, trailer rms 0.09039)
    cab onset:     t = 4.36 s
    trailer onset: t = 6.36 s
    onset lead:    +2 s (positive = cab first)
    envelope lag:  +2 s within 1 period(s) of the event, peak r 1.000
    forcing period: 2 s   envelope window: 25 samples
    onset agrees with amplitude: True

F2 real trailer roll -> expected TRAILER_ROLL_RISK
  VERDICT: TRAILER_ROLL_RISK
    cab rms is 0.189x the trailer, at or below the declared ratio 0.3333
    amplitude ratio cab/trailer: 0.1894   (cab rms 0.1205, trailer rms 0.6362)
    cab onset:     t = 6.36 s
    trailer onset: t = 4.36 s
    onset lead:    -2 s (positive = cab first)
    envelope lag:  -2 s within 1 period(s) of the event, peak r 1.000
    forcing period: 2 s   envelope window: 25 samples
    onset agrees with amplitude: True

F3 no trailer IMU -> expected TRAILER_CHANNEL_ABSENT
  VERDICT: TRAILER_CHANNEL_ABSENT
    no trailer trace. The trailer has NOT been shown to be quiet, and fault A turns on that difference: a correct reading of the cab says nothing about the body carrying the at-risk mass.

F4 clocks misaligned -> expected NOT_EVALUABLE
  VERDICT: NOT_EVALUABLE
    trace start times differ by 0.5 s, above the 0.05 s tolerance; a lead between two clocks is not a lead between two bodies

F5 two runs on a road -> expected INSUFFICIENT_RUNS
  INSUFFICIENT_RUNS on constructed-road-5 -- 2 run(s) with a trigger on this road against a declared minimum of 3. Two points give a speed and no spread, and an edge quoted without a spread is a point pretending to be a measurement.
    runs with a trigger: 2   without: 1   required: 3
    no-trigger speeds kept: [26.0]

F6 ice (addition) -> expected OUT_OF_ENVELOPE
  VERDICT: OUT_OF_ENVELOPE
    surface 'ice' is outside the declared reading set ['dry', 'wet']; on snow or ice the margin and the sensor behaviour are different and this reader does not reach them

F7 axes disagree (addition) -> expected NOT_EVALUABLE
  VERDICT: NOT_EVALUABLE
    amplitude reads GEOMETRIC_CAB_MODE while onset has the other body moving first (lead -2 s); two readings pointing opposite ways is not a verdict
    amplitude ratio cab/trailer: 6.314   (cab rms 0.6026, trailer rms 0.09544)
    cab onset:     t = 6.36 s
    trailer onset: t = 4.36 s
    onset lead:    -2 s (positive = cab first)
    envelope lag:  -2 s within 1 period(s) of the event, peak r 1.000
    forcing period: 2 s   envelope window: 25 samples
    onset agrees with amplitude: False

F8 comparable amplitudes (addition) -> expected NOT_EVALUABLE
  VERDICT: NOT_EVALUABLE
    amplitude ratio 1.15 sits between the declared bounds 0.3333 and 3; the two bodies move comparably and this record does not separate them
    amplitude ratio cab/trailer: 1.148   (cab rms 0.6362, trailer rms 0.554)
    cab onset:     t = 4.36 s
    trailer onset: t = 6.08 s
    onset lead:    +1.72 s (positive = cab first)
    envelope lag:  +1 s within 1 period(s) of the event, peak r 0.991
    forcing period: 2 s   envelope window: 25 samples

